WEBVTT

NOTE Narrated edition. Aligned to fal ElevenLabs character timestamps; natural voice speed; actual captured screens with explicit final-frame holds.

1
00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:03.499
Make an interface feel like it belongs to someone.

2
00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:10.035
In Baste, start with a persona’s films, music, spaces and working habits.

3
00:00:10.437 --> 00:00:15.132
The fitting makes that world visible through colour, type and interface details.

4
00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:18.162
Tailor a copy or measure a new persona.

5
00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.507
Give it a name and a clear description.

6
00:00:21.037 --> 00:00:25.511
Add concrete influences, values and software preferences.

7
00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:28.971
Choose the aesthetic axes and visual keywords.

8
00:00:29.443 --> 00:00:35.182
Save deliberately; the completion meter measures filled fields, not design quality.

9
00:00:35.654 --> 00:00:41.377
In Tokens, compare spacing, edges and motion, then export CSS, Tailwind,

10
00:00:41.377 --> 00:00:42.763
Panda or JSON.

11
00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:45.642
Downloaded files stay on your device.

12
00:00:45.986 --> 00:00:51.900
The demo uses built-in token examples; custom measurements do not start fresh generation.

13
00:00:52.326 --> 00:00:56.463
Build a moodboard from image references, tags and notes.

14
00:00:56.958 --> 00:01:01.223
Pin the important references; leave the notes field to save it.

15
00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:06.560
In Taste, name an asset, explain your verdict and ask for more or less of

16
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.446
that style.

17
00:01:07.755 --> 00:01:10.999
Inspect the feedback that later prompts can use.

18
00:01:11.412 --> 00:01:15.201
Start Generate with a dry run and inspect the prompt.

19
00:01:15.604 --> 00:01:19.427
This browser demo simulates jobs and makes no paid calls.

20
00:01:19.632 --> 00:01:22.225
OpenPencil edits a separate document.

21
00:01:22.628 --> 00:01:28.003
Real generation, website decomposition, native files and saved projects need the

22
00:01:28.003 --> 00:01:30.736
appropriate server or account connection.

23
00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:36.483
Explore the material room, save a recipe and reload it when you want another fitting.

24
00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:43.096
Remember: reloading Studio clears demo work, while downloads and

25
00:01:43.096 --> 00:01:45.294
material preferences survive.

26
00:01:45.662 --> 00:01:51.188
The full English and French guide documents every screen, export and connection

27
00:01:51.188 --> 00:01:51.889
boundary.
